From: Paul Spooren <mail@aparcar.org>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 05:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] udp: gro: do not keep CHECKSUM_COMPLETE on fraglist packets

udp4/6_gro_complete() leave a fraglist GRO packet CHECKSUM_COMPLETE when
its head came in that way, but skb->csum still covers the first segment
only, while uh->len now spans all of them. On local delivery,
udp4_csum_init() validates the aggregate before udp_queue_rcv_skb()
splits it: the fast check fails and, for packets up to CHECKSUM_BREAK
(76 bytes), the software fallback checksums the merged payload against
the first segment's uh->check. All segments are dropped and counted as
UDP InCsumErrors.

Seen with bcmgenet (Raspberry Pi 4), which reports CHECKSUM_COMPLETE, and
fraglist GRO enabled by default: a client's back-to-back A and AAAA DNS
queries are merged and never reach dnsmasq.

Every segment's checksum was validated in udp4/6_gro_receive() before it
was merged, so drop the stale CHECKSUM_COMPLETE and mark the packet
CHECKSUM_UNNECESSARY like one that came in as CHECKSUM_NONE.

Fixes: 9fd1ff5d2ac7 ("udp: Support UDP fraglist GRO/GSO.")
Signed-off-by: Paul Spooren <mail@aparcar.org>
---
 net/ipv4/udp_offload.c | 3 +++
 net/ipv6/udp_offload.c | 3 +++
 2 files changed, 6 insertions(+)

--- a/net/ipv4/udp_offload.c
+++ b/net/ipv4/udp_offload.c
@@ -973,6 +973,9 @@ INDIRECT_CALLABLE_SCOPE int udp4_gro_com
 		skb_shinfo(skb)->gso_type |= (SKB_GSO_FRAGLIST|SKB_GSO_UDP_L4);
 		skb_shinfo(skb)->gso_segs = NAPI_GRO_CB(skb)->count;

+		/* skb->csum covers the first segment only; all were validated */
+		if (skb->ip_summed == CHECKSUM_COMPLETE)
+			skb->ip_summed = CHECKSUM_NONE;
 		__skb_incr_checksum_unnecessary(skb);

 		return 0;
--- a/net/ipv6/udp_offload.c
+++ b/net/ipv6/udp_offload.c
@@ -178,6 +178,9 @@ INDIRECT_CALLABLE_SCOPE int udp6_gro_com
 		skb_shinfo(skb)->gso_type |= (SKB_GSO_FRAGLIST|SKB_GSO_UDP_L4);
 		skb_shinfo(skb)->gso_segs = NAPI_GRO_CB(skb)->count;

+		/* skb->csum covers the first segment only; all were validated */
+		if (skb->ip_summed == CHECKSUM_COMPLETE)
+			skb->ip_summed = CHECKSUM_NONE;
 		__skb_incr_checksum_unnecessary(skb);

 		return 0;
